id: pm-wnbk2l
title: "GH-779 recurrence: history-redact must refresh item and drift projections atomically"
description: "The audited history-redact transaction writes item and history files directly, bypassing both drift-cache invalidation and the metadata derived-index refresh used by normal item mutations. On a warmed large tracker, validation can compare rewritten history with stale item metadata and recreate a false hash mismatch after runtime GC."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:sdk",cache,context-integrity,github-report,history,privacy,regression
created_at: "2026-08-02T10:41:02.284Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T12:22:33.861Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T12:22:08.812Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T12:22:08.812Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A successful history-redact invalidates drift verification state; Rewritten or relocated items refresh the metadata derived index in the same serialized transaction; Rollback preserves authoritative files and invalidates derived drift state; A warmed-index regression proves validate sees the rewritten item and history without gc; GitHub #779 links this recurrence item
parent: pm-o2kc
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "History redaction refreshes item metadata and drift projections within the serialized transaction, including rollback invalidation"
actual_result: "Implemented, regression-covered, manually package-tested, and verified on exact-head cross-platform nightly run 30747290823"
fixed_version: next-auto-release
