comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T10:41:02.284Z","harness:codex","Duplicate guard acknowledgement: pm identified closed pm-ajaskl by the shared GH-779 code. That item remains valid completed history for the general invalidation fix; this separate child records the newly reproduced later history-redact bypass and is linked discovered_from rather than marked duplicate."
  "2026-08-02T10:43:41.590Z","harness:codex","Root cause and implementation evidence: history-redact directly rewrote authoritative item/history files outside mutateItem, so a warm metadata projection survived while drift state could also remain. The rewrite now holds the derived-index writer lock, invalidates drift state after commit or rollback, refreshes moved/updated/deleted item projections, and returns refresh warnings. Regression prewarms both caches, redacts, proves drift cache removal, then validates clean without gc."
  "2026-08-02T11:28:23.253Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide verification: 418 test files and 6,703 tests passed under the sandboxed coverage runner with exact 100% statements (47,529/47,529), branches (34,246/34,246), functions (9,673/9,673), and lines (46,119/46,119). No coverage thresholds, exclusions, or ignore counts were weakened."
  "2026-08-02T11:32:32.647Z","harness:codex","Linked-test context correction: the entire validate-command suite contains unrelated cases that intentionally scan the checkout corpus and therefore cannot run truthfully inside pm test's nested PM_PATH sandbox (11 unrelated artifact-scan failures), while it passes in the repository coverage runner. Replaced that over-broad link with the exact warmed-cache redaction regression; this preserves sandbox isolation and avoids recording unrelated failures as acceptance evidence."
  "2026-08-02T11:35:49.862Z","harness:codex","Packed-consumer acceptance: pnpm smoke:npx passed the generated tarball across 15 packaged modules. An independent tarball was then installed from unrelated root /tmp/tmp.0PKR29g4Dz into separate npm and Bun consumers with isolated project/global trackers; both initialized, created items, added evidence, and returned files lookup total=1. npm additionally proved atomic files/docs replacement and exact repeated evidence changed=false."
  "2026-08-02T11:35:50.715Z","harness:codex","Linked verification final receipt: the exact quoted warmed-cache redaction regression passed 1/1 in the PM schema sandbox. The earlier full-file linked failures were context-induced unrelated artifact-scan cases and are superseded by this precise passing link plus the separately passing full 6,703-test coverage run."
  "2026-08-02T12:21:54.082Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance: exact head fd69b84335ead8ef1022b606a470166e78c9f188 passed nightly run 30747290823 on Windows Node 24, macOS Node 24, and Ubuntu Node 22/24/25. Ubuntu Node 24 also passed secret scan, exact 100% coverage, static quality, and compatibility migration gates."
